#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
AndersXn OS - graphical installer.

A GTK4 front end over the same engine the text installer uses. It never touches
a disk itself: it drives `ax-installer` through the JSON protocol in
installer/internal/api,

    ax-installer --probe                 -> machine + catalog, as JSON
    ax-installer --run-plan <file>       -> newline-delimited progress events

which is why this is Python rather than Go. AndersXn images are routinely
cross-built, and a compiled toolkit binding (gotk4, Fyne) would drag a full
cross-compiled GTK stack into the build for no benefit. PyGObject needs no
compilation, so the graphical front end costs the build nothing and stays
readable - and patchable - on the live medium itself.

The GUI runs unprivileged. Only the install step escalates, through sudo (the
live session has a NOPASSWD rule) or pkexec.
"""

